Blocks opened and never closed at end of file: a :PROCEDURE whose :IF
and :WHILE have no closers and no :ENDPROC. Each unclosed opener should
be reported once; indentation stays nested to the end.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE Unfinished;
:PARAMETERS nValue;
:IF nValue > 0;
:WHILE nValue > 0;
nValue -= 1;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE Unfinished;
	:PARAMETERS nValue;
	:IF nValue > 0;
		:WHILE nValue > 0;
			nValue -= 1;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
3:1-3:4 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
4:1-4:7 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':WHILE' - expected ':ENDWHILE'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:11 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':PROCEDURE' - expected ':ENDPROC'
3:1-3:4 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':IF' - expected ':ENDIF'
4:1-4:7 error unclosed_block: Unclosed ':WHILE' - expected ':ENDWHILE'
